---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HVAC Training Solutions | Start Learning HVAC the Right Way"
  description="Beginner-friendly online HVAC training that helps you understand the fundamentals, prepare for interviews, and get support when you are stuck."
>
  <div class="home-page">
    <section class="home-hero">
      <div class="home-hero-inner">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A clearer way into the HVAC trade</p>
          <h1>Learn HVAC from the ground up. <span>Understand the fundamentals technicians use every day.</span></h1>
          <p class="home-hero-lead">Build the fundamentals, practice explaining what you know, and prepare for an entry-level HVAC opportunity—with a real instructor and focused learning help behind you.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-primary" href="/try-boot-camp/">Try a lesson first</a>
            <a class="button button-light" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Explore HVAC Boot Camp</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-fineprint">No HVAC experience required · Learn online · Instructor support included</p>
        </div>

        <aside class="start-card" aria-label="Choose your next step">
          <p class="start-card-kicker">Where are you right now?</p>
          <a href="/try-boot-camp/"><span>01</span><div><strong>I am completely new to HVAC</strong><small>See how the first lesson explains the basics.</small></div><b>→</b></a>
          <a href="/how-it-works/"><span>02</span><div><strong>I want to know how the training works</strong><small>See the lesson, support, and career-prep path.</small></div><b>→</b></a>
          <a href="/pricing/"><span>03</span><div><strong>I am ready to compare plans</strong><small>Review the full-pay and monthly options.</small></div><b>→</b></a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="HVAC Boot Camp highlights">
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div class="proof-item"><strong>27 modules</strong><span>A structured technical foundation</span></div>
        <div class="proof-item"><strong>Beginner friendly</strong><span>Starts with the basics</span></div>
        <div class="proof-item"><strong>Instructor support</strong><span>You are not left alone</span></div>
        <div class="proof-item"><strong>Career preparation</strong><span>From learning to interview</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <div class="page-shell split-feature">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">The problem with most online training</p>
          <h2>Watching is not the same as understanding.</h2>
          <p>A difficult HVAC concept can stop your progress long before the quiz. Boot Camp is being rebuilt around the moments when learners usually get lost.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="friction-list">
          <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Too much at once</h3><p>Lessons are broken into small concepts so you can focus on one idea before moving on.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>02</span><div><h3>No help at the point of confusion</h3><p>Focused assistance explains the current page more simply or connects it to an HVAC example.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>03</span><div><h3>No bridge to employment</h3><p>Technical learning connects to employer research, an OJT plan, and interview preparation.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section soft-section">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="section-heading center">
          <p class="eyebrow">A simple learning rhythm</p>
          <h2>Learn it. Work with it. Check it. Move on.</h2>
          <p>The student should always know what to focus on and what the next action is.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="process-grid">
          <article><span>1</span><h3>One clear concept</h3><p>Read or watch only what is needed for the idea in front of you.</p></article>
          <article><span>2</span><h3>Help when needed</h3><p>Ask for a simpler explanation, an HVAC example, or why it matters.</p></article>
          <article><span>3</span><h3>A quick check</h3><p>Answer a focused question and get immediate feedback.</p></article>
          <article><span>4</span><h3>Visible progress</h3><p>Move forward knowing what you completed and where to continue.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="center-actions"><a class="button button-dark" href="/try-boot-camp/">Try the learning experience</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="home-offer">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">The complete starting point</p>
            <h2>HVAC Boot Camp</h2>
            <p>Twenty-seven modules covering fundamentals, refrigeration, tools, safety, airflow, electricity, troubleshooting, heating, and heat pumps—plus instructor support and career preparation.</p>
            <div class="offer-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">See everything included</a><a class="text-link-dark" href="/pricing/">Compare payment options →</a></div>
          </div>
          <ul class="offer-list">
            <li><strong>Start from the beginning</strong><span>No prior HVAC experience required.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Study around your schedule</strong><span>Online access with a structured path.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Get unstuck</strong><span>Learning help plus access to Ron.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Prepare for the next step</strong><span>Employer search, OJT plan, and interview practice.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section proof-section soft-section">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <div class="section-heading center"><p class="eyebrow">Student experience</p><h2>Understanding gives you something real to talk about.</h2></div>
        <div class="student-proof-grid">
          <article class="testimonial-card"><p class="testimonial-text">Robert said a prospective employer was impressed when he discussed the refrigeration cycle, pressures, temperatures, subcooling, and superheat. He was offered a job.</p><p class="testimonial-name">— Robert O.</p></article>
          <article class="testimonial-card"><p class="testimonial-text">Chris said he could explain the refrigeration cycle in detail during an interview even though his hands-on gauge experience was still limited.</p><p class="testimonial-name">— Chris J.</p></article>
        </div>
        <p class="result-disclaimer">Student experiences vary. HVAC Training Solutions does not guarantee employment.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section final-cta">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Do not take our word for it</p>
        <h2>Try one concept before you choose the course.</h2>
        <p>See whether the short, focused lesson style works for you. No account or payment is required for the preview.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/try-boot-camp/">Try a lesson</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/">See pricing</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
